{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_—_Modular_Arithmetic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 — Modular Arithmetic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:_Answer_choices\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4: Answer choices</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(modular_congruences)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (modular congruences)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Because_it_doesn&#39;t_have_to_be_that_complicated)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Because it doesn't have to be that complicated)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Brain_Math_Club\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Brain Math Club</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_RMM_Club\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by RMM Club</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Vincent_Lo\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Vincent Lo</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math_Ex\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math Ex</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After Euclid High School's last basketball game, it was determined that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the team's points were scored by Alexa and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726bdcb0779fcb4723bfc790d0f677a9981261a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> were scored by Brittany. Chelsea scored <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points. None of the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> team members scored more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points. What was the total number of points scored by the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> team members?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744deec89cb020a27de934a7e1affe73f8cfb1d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }11\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }12\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }13\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the information above, we start with the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf6396f3da3b5134d967d904e7f446e160f0822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{4}+\\frac{2t}{7} + 15 + x = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the total number of points scored and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3225d72bd01be1666e12c6687deb68129c7e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\le 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of points scored by the remaining 7 team members, we can simplify to obtain the Diophantine equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bccffdaf6f9624a88376ccae4382067a0420d3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+15 = \\frac{13}{28}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b726773be9699af3dec8f06eaec680d2f3f3c888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28x+28\\cdot 15=13t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is necessarily divisible by 28, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed105082650bd958ea06db6898d21003df920b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=28u$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374964881cded81afd80e25a72ee2fa9e93f0295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and divide by 28 to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3766bdd3848540510c936708c6df582ad4e05f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 15 = 13u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. Then, it is easy to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/013399c030c302417bdbba2f03e2416c1c449135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83d7a5d2e9f00f4c8a8deca7ddf86e1abc1fa73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=56$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />) is the only candidate remaining, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c41e1abb09183c41755f2d0bbf2d2c86c7db9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"93\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>-DummyAMC\n~Minor Edits by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Wrenmath\" title=\"User:Wrenmath\">Wrenmath</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first start by setting the total number of points as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5283b0501319268e82fcf9cff767d7e588b84ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{LCM}(4,7) = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. However, we see that this does not work since we surpass the number of points just with the information given (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da7a8ed7e74c538cb584a5a477ba7f9407394c3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}+28\\cdot\\frac{2}{7} + 15 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654e7ddc13b814768379ae8c8888d23cbbd76648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(&gt; 28)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> ). Next, we can see that the total number of points scored is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> as, if it is more than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, at least one of the others will score more than 2 points. With this, we have that Alexa, Brittany, and Chelsea score: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e20bb2d28c4ac65ebeec5ce80d88e7cbc1c9eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}+56\\cdot\\frac{2}{7} + 15 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"196\" height=\"38\" />, and thus, the other seven players would have scored a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d33da596cc2d09f235120c0874ebcd8b748fcc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56-45 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"141\" height=\"28\" />. (We see that this works since we could have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them score <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them score <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point.) \n</p><p>-aops5234 -Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Penguin_Spellcaster\" title=\"User:Penguin Spellcaster\">Penguin_Spellcaster</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.E2.80.94_Modular_Arithmetic\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_—_Modular_Arithmetic\">Solution 3 — Modular Arithmetic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 — Modular Arithmetic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Adding together Alexa's and Brittany's fractions, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c903ea682113e9cbf033197d6b85d732bc59ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> as the fraction of the total number of points they scored together. However, this is just a ratio, so we can introduce a variable: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045a5aac0b8600166b219b68f16046d44c3cd4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15x}{28x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the common ratio. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of people who scored 1, 2, and 0 points, respectively. Writing an equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8daac22b363d35194aaf97bc44541e96db81fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13x}{28x} = 15 + y + 2z + 0w.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" /> We want all of our variables to be integers. Thus, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d4cd18a0e8a1b856a521ed7ca15b7b7a8ac944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + y + 2z = 0 \\pmod {13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" /> Simplifying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d123b87ea2ab6e94d17c09f19c4e92b8ab6ccad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+2z = 11 \\pmod {13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" /> The only possible value, as this integer sum has to be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13460005e98460fc7e1f6b86448feadf8a85aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 2 + 1 = 15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> must be 11. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d5343d30a764f8285a722472d38e841c4f062ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+2z = 11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/6647e17101b46ebb24eee7b93a39bbae874f6fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ \\textbf{(B) 11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>- ab2024\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:_Answer_choices\">Solution 4: Answer choices</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4: Answer choices\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite the question as an algebraic equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b9b65030f5bd2f37c1c15f80631fd967707908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} T + \\frac{2}{7} T + 15 + y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> represents the total amount of points and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> the amount of points the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other players scored. From there, we add the two fractions to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5309afe3a53b8afc6403f995094799b6c7f409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{28} x + 15 + y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" />. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1be1880bf42891fa3edf714f4001856a762f212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{28} x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" /> from both sides, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944854a77c29081c484e02f5d2886fec8e00afc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{28} x = y + 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />. We multiply each side by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get rid of the denominator, in which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2ac7b74fed6b1d4dc92ce28ce964a8a14a7b9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13x = 420 + 28y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />. Now let’s think of this logically. This equation is telling us that if you add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb2fec2f1cde0059d8eb9c11bcb2bd63142401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the amount of points scored by the extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> players, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the amount of points total. And since we have to have a whole number of points total, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3710328b9ba7ceca4094f68ebfd3f35982747121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420 + 28y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging in all the answer choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we find that the only answer that makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3710328b9ba7ceca4094f68ebfd3f35982747121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420 + 28y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/6647e17101b46ebb24eee7b93a39bbae874f6fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ \\textbf{(B) 11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ilee0820\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28modular_congruences.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(modular_congruences)\">Solution 5 (modular congruences)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (modular congruences)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in the above, we can write the equation \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b13d61e741f42494769e1f9c01d5974776ff635.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{4}k+\\frac{2}{7}k+15+y=k\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"37\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the total points, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the rest of the students' total. This simplifies to the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821a68d7b5b1c67a445391614b99451d8a977004.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y+15=\\frac{13}{28}k \\implies\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e994bf6d2b8821e99cf8c4766a26f12df197a9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[28y+15 \\cdot 28 = 13k\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437613cd7d1b76e0cb6e037c3dc855c2951dea89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are both integers, we have the modular congruence equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c264347cb93ff8b8aa7240659af032e42ee8749.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[28y+15 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{13} \\implies\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a5490b0537258049bc48e735015f8bc63e2908fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2y \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\nSince the modular inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f3692baf9b4f81463303d93e31e9bf00b10fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this simplifies to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43a197aa7434c05b8f1f99ccee79825889f263f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y \\equiv 11 \\cdot 7 \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />\nThe question asks for the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925942db2484375cd6f565061bc5da54d8e6748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"60\" height=\"32\" /> <br /> \n~iretra\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Because_it_doesn.27t_have_to_be_that_complicated.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Because_it_doesn't_have_to_be_that_complicated)\">Solution 6 (Because it doesn't have to be that complicated)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Because it doesn&#39;t have to be that complicated)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know from the problem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e79afcdc024e87e30038ca4907c0bc5d57a51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> of the points are already taken. Then we add them together yielding, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c903ea682113e9cbf033197d6b85d732bc59ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, which means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72d88efa87d80164762217fb2d4bceb97e9fdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> points left. Here is the magic part: Multiply it by 56, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. And now we can subtract Chelsea's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points. That leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925942db2484375cd6f565061bc5da54d8e6748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"60\" height=\"32\" /> <br />\nP.S. Why do we multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />? Since the answer is a whole number we have to multiply by a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We try different value and find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is too small and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4131457f67c5dbfd8b1c6be1f74a47595a9bd3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> is too big. <br />\n~Fluffy1234\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X\">Video Solution by Math-X</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=JjQHbrlBpeox9TFq&amp;t=9178\">https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=JjQHbrlBpeox9TFq&amp;t=9178</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Brain_Math_Club\">Video Solution by Brain Math Club</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Brain Math Club\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fKjmw_zzCUU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fKjmw_zzCUU</a> \n</p><p>- Happytwin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_RMM_Club\">Video Solution by RMM Club</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by RMM Club\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jE-7Se7ay1c\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jE-7Se7ay1c</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Mae_6qFxoU&amp;t\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Mae_6qFxoU&amp;t</a> \n</p><p>~ hi_im_bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Vincent_Lo\">Video Solution by Vincent Lo</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Vincent Lo\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wsYCn2FqZJE\">https://youtu.be/wsYCn2FqZJE</a>\n</p><p>~Vincent Lo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math_Ex\">Video Solution by Math Ex</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math Ex\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o2mcnLOVFBA&amp;list=PLLCzevlMcsWNBsdpItBT4r7Pa8cZb6Viu&amp;index=5\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o2mcnLOVFBA&amp;list=PLLCzevlMcsWNBsdpItBT4r7Pa8cZb6Viu&amp;index=5</a> \n</p><p>~ MathEx\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Omega Learn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=4115\">https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=4115</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dI8RzUHLqZc\">https://youtu.be/dI8RzUHLqZc</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Proble